Incompatible changes with snapshot 20260502
===========================================

TLS is now mandatory. This Postfix build refuses to send or accept
mail over an unencrypted SMTP channel; cleartext SMTP is no longer
supported. There is no configuration parameter to opt out.

Outbound (smtp client): the policy resolver promotes any sub-ENCRYPT
level (NONE, MAY, per-site overrides, sender "TLS-Required: no"
header downgrades) to ENCRYPT. The remote peer must offer STARTTLS;
a failed handshake defers the message instead of falling back to
cleartext. Mail to any recipient whose MX does not offer STARTTLS
will defer until the queue lifetime expires and the message bounces.

Inbound (smtpd server): smtpd_check_init unconditionally forces
smtpd_use_tls, smtpd_enforce_tls, and smtpd_tls_auth_only to "yes",
overriding smtpd_tls_security_level. The server advertises STARTTLS,
rejects all plaintext commands except those allowed before STARTTLS
(HELO, EHLO, XCLIENT, STARTTLS, NOOP, QUIT, HELP), and refuses AUTH
before TLS. A port-25 listener built from this tree will reject mail
from any peer that does not offer STARTTLS, in violation of RFC 2487
and RFC 3207. This is intentional.

Exception: "sendmail -bs" runs unprivileged with no access to the
server private key. In that mode TLS is bypassed and local-IPC
submission continues to work.

Configuration parameters smtp_tls_security_level and
smtpd_tls_security_level remain honored for authentication strictness
(encrypt / dane / verify / secure on the client side, encrypt on the
server). Settings of "none" or "may" are silently treated as "encrypt".

The smtp_allow_plaintext_session / smtpd_allow_plaintext_session
parameters that briefly existed during development of this branch
have been removed; the behavior they enabled is now hard-wired.

Incompatible changes with snapshot 20260312
===========================================

For consistency with postmap, the postalias command now stores the
alias database search key in external (quoted) form. For example,
if an alias name contains whitespace between the words 'foo' and
'bar', then it will be stored as "foo bar" including the double
quotes.

For consistency with "postmap -s", the "postalias -s" command now
outputs the search key in external (quoted) form.

For backwards compatibility, the local(8) delivery agent will look
up the legacy internal (unquoted) form of an alias name only if the
preferred external (quoted) form is not found, and the internal and
external forms differ.
